---
import CourseLayout from "../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import DossierTools from "../../components/DossierTools.astro";
import {crew,activities} from "../../data/academy";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
---
<CourseLayout title="The Operation Room" description="Your evidence, crew, plans and rehearsal records. One local dossier; every training week remains open." eyebrow="OPERATION 408 / GLASS CROWN" wide>
<div class="actions no-print"><a class="button" href="#journal">Read dossier</a><a class="button" href="#plans">Compare plans</a><a class="button" href="#rehearsal">Run a rehearsal</a></div>
<div class="workspace-grid"><div><DossierTools/><section id="journal" data-dossier><h2>Fieldwork journal</h2><p>Enable JavaScript to view locally saved responses. All lab worksheets remain available from the week links.</p></section><section id="plans" data-plan-comparison><h2>Plan comparison</h2><p>Week 6 preserves Version 1. Week 7 creates Version 2; direct visitors receive a labelled sample original.</p></section></div>
<aside><section class="workbench"><h2>Open a training file</h2><ol>{activities.map(a=><li><a href={withBase("/sessions/week-"+String(a.week).padStart(2,"0")+"/")}>{a.title}</a></li>)}</ol></section><section class="workbench"><h2>Crew roster</h2><p class="small">Select a roster here; record responsibilities and consent in Weeks 5 and 9. Selection alone is not agreement.</p>{crew.map(c=><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" value={c.id} data-crew/><span><strong>{c.name}</strong><br/>{c.role}</span></label>)}<button type="button" data-save-crew disabled>Save roster</button></section></aside></div>
<section id="rehearsal" class="workbench"><p class="eyebrow">THE RIVAL'S REHEARSAL</p><h2>Six decisions. A record you can defend.</h2><p>Start a named preset. The rules are explicit and the outcome is reproducible. The ending is never an academic grade.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" data-start-run="baseline" disabled>Start Baseline</button><button type="button" data-start-run="contradiction" disabled>Start Contradiction</button><button type="button" data-start-run="divided-crew" disabled>Start Divided Crew</button></div><div data-rehearsal aria-live="polite"><p>Enable JavaScript to run the rehearsal. The six decisions and rules are available below as a worksheet.</p></div>
<details><summary>Rehearsal rules and paper alternative</summary><p>Use twelve decision units. Declare extraction, disclosure or withdrawal. Inspect E02 (2 units) or assume its causal claim (1 unit, two unresolved assumptions). Renew crew agreement in council (2 units, agreement +1) or proceed with assigned roles (1 unit, agreement −1).</p><p>Baseline and Divided Crew use R1. Contradiction issues R2: revising costs 2 units; retaining the old model costs 1 unit and adds two unresolved assumptions. Examine E10 for 1 unit, or leave it unresolved and add an assumption. Declaring the initial and final objectives costs one unit each.</p><p>Agreement begins at 2, or 1 for Divided Crew. More than two unresolved assumptions, no agreement, or a negative budget prevents extraction or disclosure and ends in withdrawal. Record all six choices and explain them using E01, E02, E05/E09, E03/E07, E10 and E12. Compare two presets.</p></details></section>
<section data-run-history></section>
</CourseLayout>
